{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "Init marks the explicit process start; action n1 faithfully restates the initial return step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2",
        "guard:b1->n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process. However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n2 formulates the routing decision; branch b1 splits the flow; the guards capture both exact conditional phrases."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct, faithful restatement of the inventory comparison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n4 poses the order status decision; branch b2 correctly models the three-way conditional split."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges"
      ],
      "justification": "Exact reproduction of the damage notification instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the missing-items email step without adding or dropping qualifiers."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b3->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process. However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n6 frames the return question; branch b3 and guards implement both exact outcomes."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit closure statement mapped to the terminal action and structural end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12",
        "guard:b4->n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the repair-status decision, both literal outcomes, the resulting email action, and the positive-branch guard."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the final packing/storage decision point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends. The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the concluding replacement-charges email step."
    }
  ],
